1. DISTINGUISH MISSING RPC FIELDS FROM LEGITIMATE ZERO VALUES
=============================================================

The current Raw* DTO structs use ordinary Go numeric/string zero values for
many fields Core always emits.

That makes malformed/partial RPC JSON indistinguishable from legitimate
values.

Examples:

ordinary vin with missing "vout"
  currently becomes vout=0

missing "sequence"
  currently becomes sequence=0

missing transaction "locktime"
  currently becomes locktime=0

missing block "nonce"
  currently becomes nonce=0

All of these zero values can legitimately occur, so value-based checking
cannot solve this.

Introduce explicit field-presence tracking for REQUIRED Core wire fields.

A straightforward solution is pointer fields in the raw DTOs, though a
small custom required-field type/custom UnmarshalJSON is acceptable if it
keeps the DTO cleaner.

Required transaction fields include:

  txid
  hash
  version
  size
  vsize
  weight
  locktime
  vin
  vout

Required ordinary vin fields:

  txid
  vout
  scriptSig
  sequence

Required coinbase vin fields:

  coinbase
  sequence

Required vout fields:

  value
  n
  scriptPubKey

Required scriptPubKey member:

  hex

Required block fields include:

  hash
  height
  merkleroot
